    "title": "Bamboo poles and boomboxes: The kanwar yatra's ancient roots, faith and modern-day frictions | Hindustan Times",
    "text": "What is the kanwar yatra?\nIn Bihar, Jharkhand, Uttar Pradesh and Odisha, the pilgrimage is popularly called the Bol Bam Yatra. Devotees travel on foot to collect Gangajal from sacred sites, chiefly Gaumukh, Gangotri and Haridwar in Uttarakhand, and Sultanganj in Bihar’s Bhagalpur district. Sultanganj holds particular significance as one of the few points where the Ganga flows northward — known as Uttarvahini Ganga.",
